[2026-09-20 13:01:39 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 113] STEP PURPOSE
[2026-09-20 13:01:39 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 113] --------------------------------------------------------------------------------
[2026-09-20 13:01:39 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 113]   Step 113 -- Independent-survey resident ledger.
[2026-09-20 13:01:39 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 113]   The resident signature now stands on three detached-TNO cohorts drawn
[2026-09-20 13:01:39 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 113]   by three independent survey selections and three independent orbit
[2026-09-20 13:01:39 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 113]   determinations:
[2026-09-20 13:01:39 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 113]   SBDB (JPL):      the 44-object secure detached cohort (a>150, q>30,
[2026-09-20 13:01:39 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 113]   condition code <=3); orbit lineage JPL/MPC;
[2026-09-20 13:01:39 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 113]   designation-proxy footprint baseline.
[2026-09-20 13:01:39 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 113]   DES (Bernardinelli et al. 2022): the 16-object detached cohort from
[2026-09-20 13:01:39 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 113]   a single 5000 deg^2 southern survey; DES-team orbit
[2026-09-20 13:01:39 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 113]   fits; designation-proxy footprint baseline
[2026-09-20 13:01:39 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 113]   (step_085).
[2026-09-20 13:01:39 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 113]   OSSOS (Bannister et al. 2018): the 31-object 'det' cohort from the
[2026-09-20 13:01:39 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 113]   only fully characterized TNO survey; OSSOS-team
[2026-09-20 13:01:39 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 113]   fits; EXACT discovery astrometry -- the footprint
[2026-09-20 13:01:39 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 113]   baseline here is measured from the table's own
[2026-09-20 13:01:39 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 113]   discovery RA/Dec, not proxied (step_112).
[2026-09-20 13:01:39 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 113]   This step scores each cohort identically against the pre-declared
[2026-09-20 13:01:39 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 113]   axis (lam,beta) = (49,-17) deg, cap 60 deg, against each cohort's own
[2026-09-20 13:01:39 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 113]   footprint baseline, and combines them three ways:
[2026-09-20 13:01:39 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 113]   1.  Fisher's method on the per-cohort p_vs_baseline values -- the
[2026-09-20 13:01:39 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 113]   honest combination when the cohorts share members (their
[2026-09-20 13:01:39 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 113]   selection functions, not their memberships, are independent).
[2026-09-20 13:01:39 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 113]   2.  A deduplicated union pool: each distinct object counted once,
[2026-09-20 13:01:39 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 113]   assigned the baseline of its primary survey; a single binomial
[2026-09-20 13:01:39 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 113]   test of the union in-cap count, reported for the full pool and
[2026-09-20 13:01:39 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 113]   for the boundary-resident subset (a>150) on which the resident
[2026-09-20 13:01:39 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 113]   anomaly is defined.
[2026-09-20 13:01:39 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 113]   3.  Direction concordance: the in-cap members' mean varpi per
[2026-09-20 13:01:39 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 113]   survey, tested for mutual consistency against the footprint
[2026-09-20 13:01:39 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 113]   null (does each survey's in-cap population point at the same
[2026-09-20 13:01:39 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 113]   place?).
[2026-09-20 13:01:39 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 113]   Membership overlap is handled explicitly: DES has 14/16 objects in
[2026-09-20 13:01:39 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 113]   SBDB, OSSOS-det has 9 named designations of which 9 match SBDB; the
[2026-09-20 13:01:39 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 113]   ledger reports the overlap so no independence is overclaimed.  The
[2026-09-20 13:01:39 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 113]   OSSOS 'det' class is dominated by a ~50-90 AU orbits -- interior to
[2026-09-20 13:01:39 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 113]   the ~150 AU boundary -- so its role in the ledger is a selection-
[2026-09-20 13:01:39 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 113]   function bound, not a high-leverage replication.
